er over the grave",s:"The Round Stones",s:"The belief that the deep iron angers the ancestors",s:"The Ban of the Living Trees",s:"The Ban of the Deep Iron",s:"The Peace of Kin",s:"Humming at Dawn",s:"The Carried Stick",],"taboos":[],"beliefs":[],"conversions":n:40935c0000000000,"hunts":n:4043800000000000,"harshWinters":n:4046000000000000,"reformations":n:4000000000000000,"worldview":s:"none","tabooBreaks":n:4043000000000000,"religions":[undef,s:"The Way of the Water",],"legends":[s:"Eira Eira the Firebringer.",s:"Ask Ask the Rememberer.",s:"Rune Rune the Founder.",s:"Freja Freja the Founder.",s:"Ronja Ronja the Founder.",s:"Ylva Ylva the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"Maja Maja the Founder.",s:"Idun Idun the Voice of Majaheim.",],"milestones":{"⚙️ Storytelling":s:"year 1","⚙️ Fire":s:"year 1","⚙️ Rope":s:"year 2","⚙️ Pottery":s:"year 2","⚙️ Writing":s:"year 2","👶 First child":s:"year 2","⚙️ Sharpened stone":s:"year 2","⚙️ Spear":s:"year 3","⚙️ Axe":s:"year 3","⚙️ Hut":s:"year 3","⚙️ Bow":s:"year 3","⚙️ Kiln":s:"year 4","⚙️ Farming":s:"year 4","⚙️ Granary":s:"year 4","⚙️ Weaving":s:"year 5","⚙️ Brick":s:"year 5","⚙️ Well":s:"year 5","⚙️ Tin":s:"year 6","⚙️ The Wheel":s:"year 7","⚙️ Sailing":s:"year 7","⚙️ Fishing":s:"year 10","⚙️ Mill":s:"year 11","⚙️ Music":s:"year 12","⚙️ Counting":s:"year 12","⚙️ Calendar":s:"year 12","⚙️ Medicine":s:"year 12","⚙️ Painting":s:"year 17","⚙️ Glass":s:"year 20","🏘️ First village":s:"year 33","🌿 First tradition":s:"year 35","⚙️ Copper":s:"year 54","⚙️ Iron smithing":s:"year 137","⚙️ Metal tools":s:"year 139","⛩️ First religion":s:"year 145","⚙️ Philosophy":s:"year 173","⚙️ Masonry":s:"year 176","⚙️ Law":s:"year 183","⚙️ School":s:"year 183","⚙️ Composition":s:"year 183","⚙️ Coal":s:"year 186","⚙️ Glassblowing":s:"year 191","⚙️ Road":s:"year 237","⚙️ Architecture":s:"year 238","⚙️ Aqueduct":s:"year 268","⚙️ Steel":s:"year 308","⚙️ Coinage":s:"year 313","⚙️ Scholarship":s:"year 344","⚙️ Temple":s:"year 347","⚙️ Optics":s:"year 361","⚙️ Windmill":s:"year 412","⚙️ University":s:"year 514","⚙️ Science":s:"year 531",},"status":s:"Extinct in year 661","violence":{"steals":n:4072d00000000000,"raids":n:4075400000000000,"feuds":n:404c000000000000,"killings":n:402a000000000000,"brawls":n:4085c80000000000,"wars":n:4050400000000000,},"trades":n:4089980000000000,"gifts":n:408e000000000000,"leaders":[],"giftWays":[s:"Runestead: The Hearth-Gift",s:"Frejaheim: The Full Bowl Custom",s:"Ronjastead: The Shared Bowl",s:"Majaheim: The Full Bowl Custom",s:"Alveheim: The Full Bowl Custom",],"wealthTop":s:"none",},"history":{"worldName":s:"Runestead","seed":n:40a2260000000000,"years":n:4084a80000000000,"intro":s:"This is the chronicle of Runestead - 661 years, 26 generations, written by no one. Every line below happened.","outro":s:"Here the chronicle ends. The world stands silent, but it remembers.","chapters":[{"title":s:"The Waking","from":n:3ff0000000000000,"to":n:403e000000000000,"text":[s:"🌍 Four humans wake in an untouched world: Eira, Ask, Embla, Torv. They know nothing — but they can observe everything. What will they create?",s:"The chronicle marks the year 1, when Eira told the day back as a story worth remembering. Eira's the tale entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 1, when Eira rubbed sticks together until a spark caught the tinder. Eira's ember entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 2, when Embla twisted grass fibers into something strong. Embla's braid entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 2, when Ask placed shaped clay in the fire and found it hard as stone. Ask's urn entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 2, when Ask carved signs into clay so knowledge could outlive its owner. Ask's script entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 2, when Ask struck two stones together and kept the sharp shard. Ask's knife entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 3, when Ask lashed a sharp point to a long shaft. Ask's javelin entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 3, when Embla bound a hard edge to a wooden shaft. Embla's cleaver entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 3, when Ask raised logs against each other into a shelter. Ask's lodge entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 3, when Ask bent a young branch with a cord and felt it fight back. Ask's longbow entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 4, when Ask built a stone chamber that gathered the heat of the fire. Ask's hearth entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 4, when Embla pressed spilled seeds into turned soil and waited. Embla's seedcraft entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 4, when Ask built a dry raised store so the harvest kept till spring. Ask's silo entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 5, when Embla crossed threads over threads until cloth grew on the frame. Embla's the loom entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 5, when Embla fired shaped clay into blocks that stack true. Embla's mudbrick entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 5, when Ask lined a deep pit with stone to hold clean water. Ask's stone well entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 6, when Ask smelted a pale metal too soft to be worth much alone. Ask's the pale metal entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 7, when Ask watched a log roll and understood something great. Ask's roller entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 7, when Ask stretched cloth on a hull and let the wind do the work. Ask's the sail entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 10, when Ask let a twisted line sink where the fish gather. Ask's fishing line entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 11, when Eira let the wheel drive stones that ground grain. Eira's millhouse entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 12, when Ask found that a struck string and a voice could ring together. Ask's melody entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 12, when Ask matched pebble to sheep and found number itself. Ask's number entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 12, when Ask counted the stars and seasons into a fixed wheel of days. Ask's the year-wheel entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 12, when Ask learned which leaves ease pain and close a wound. Ask's the healer entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 17, when Ask ground coloured earth and left an image on the wall. Ask's cave-marks entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 20, when Ask melted sand and found something transparent. Ask's lenswork entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 1, Ask began seeing the world differently - believing the stars are the eyes of the ancestors, so the dead are never wholly gone. Where others saw patterns, they felt a will behind them.",s:"In the year 3, Embla began seeing the world differently - believing the world repeats and can be understood. Where others saw spirits, they saw patterns.",s:"The winter of year 18 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Eira was known as Eira the Firebringer.",s:"From that day on, Ask was known as Ask the Rememberer.",s:"The year 24 knew open greed: Ylva set upon Eira the Firebringer and seized goods — the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"In these years 9 children were born under its skies and 1 lives ended - 1 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:403f000000000000,"to":n:404e000000000000,"text":[s:"It was in the year 54, when Halvar coaxed a soft red metal out of green stone in the kiln. Halvar's red metal entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 33, three huts grew into more, and Runestead was founded - a place with a name, which is the beginning of belonging.",s:"In the year 41, three huts grew into more, and Frejaheim was founded - a place with a name, which is the beginning of belonging.",s:"In the year 58, three huts grew into more, and Ronjastead was founded - a place with a name, which is the beginning of belonging.",s:"By the year 35, believing the stars are the eyes of the ancestors, so the dead are never wholly gone had become simply what one does in Runestead. It merely became true.",s:"By the year 35, painting a mark on an old tree when something new is made had become simply what one does in Runestead. No council voted.",s:"By the year 35, believing the world repeats and can be understood had become simply what one does in Runestead. It merely became true.",s:"The winter of year 32 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 50 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Rune was known as Rune the Founder.",s:"From that day on, Freja was known as Freja the Founder.",s:"From that day on, Ronja was known as Ronja the Founder.",s:"Bjorn reached Frejaheim. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"The chronicle notes, without explanation, that Ask has begun collecting round stones. No one knows why. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Ask the Rememberer speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 7 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"The year 41 knew open greed: Saga set upon Liv and seized goods — the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"Through it all 16 children were born under its skies and 2 lives ended - 2 to age.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:404e800000000000,"to":n:4056800000000000,"text":[s:"In the year 73, three huts grew into more, and Majaheim was founded - a place with a name, which is the beginning of belonging.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 61, Embla — the last soul who understood painting — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 61, Embla — the last soul who understood painting — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 62, Embla — the last soul who understood tin — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 62, Embla — the last soul who understood tin — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 63, Embla — the last soul who understood tin — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 63, Embla — the last soul who understood painting — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 86, Embla — the last soul who understood painting — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Yet in the year 83 it returned - painting, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"The winter of year 63 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 80 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Ylva was known as Ylva the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"From that day on, Maja was known as Maja the Founder.",s:"From that day on, Idun was known as Idun the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Signe was known as Signe the Rekindler.",s:"Ylva the Voice of Ronjastead is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"Disa is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"And in those same years, Sixten stops at the same strange stone every day, and looks at it. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Ask's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Ylva speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Ylva's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Idun speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Runestead, the giving has become a way with a name: The Hearth-Gift — those who keep the same ways do not let each other starve. No price is asked; the gift itself binds.",s:"In Frejaheim, the giving has become a way with a name: The Full Bowl Custom — those who keep the same ways do not let each other starve. No price is asked; the gift itself binds.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 12 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 16 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"The year 88 paid an old debt: Idun the Voice of Majaheim came for Saga II — an old wrong, not forgotten, paid back in goods and bruises. Blood remembers.",s:"Through it all 34 children were born under its skies and 12 lives ended - 6 to age, 6 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4056c00000000000,"to":n:405e000000000000,"text":[s:"By the year 96, pouring water over the fallen prey had become simply what one does in Majaheim. It merely became true.",s:"By the year 104, whistling to greet the morning had become simply what one does in Runestead. No one decided this.",s:"By the year 104, pouring water over the fallen prey had become simply what one does in Majaheim. No council voted.",s:"By the year 105, planting a seed by the newborn's doorstep had become simply what one does in Runestead. It merely became true.",s:"By the year 112, pouring water over the grave had become simply what one does in Runestead. It merely became true.",s:"By the year 112, believing the living trees remember the axe had become simply what one does in Runestead. It merely became true.",s:"In Runestead, fewer and fewer keep Pouring water over the fallen prey. An age is quietly ending.",s:"The winter of year 95 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 117 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Embla II was known as Embla II the Voice of Frejaheim.",s:"From that day on, Halvar was known as Halvar the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Torv II was known as Torv II the Voice of Frejaheim.",s:"From that day on, Sixten was known as Sixten the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"Saga is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ronja the Founder is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"Sixten the Voice of Majaheim is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ask II reached Runestead. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"And in those same years, Tuva II always sits farthest from the fire. It began the year Orm died. It has not stopped since.",s:"In Frejaheim, the people have begun to listen when Embla II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Halvar speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Frejaheim is without a leader — Embla II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Frejaheim, the people have begun to listen when Torv II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Idun's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Sixten speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Halvar's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Sixten's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the giving has become a way with a name: The Full Bowl Custom — those who keep the same ways do not let each other starve. No price is asked; the gift itself binds.",s:"In Ronjastead, the giving has become a way with a name: The Shared Bowl — those who keep the same ways do not let each other starve. No price is asked; the gift itself binds.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 23 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 56 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"The year 117 paid an old debt: Freja II came for Ulv II — an old wrong, not forgotten, paid back in goods and bruises. Blood remembers.",s:"Nor were those the only debts: 6 old wrongs were paid in blood that age.",s:"Disa II mourns Embla II — and does not forget whose hand it was. Grief like that does not fade; it waits.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"16 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Through it all 75 children were born under its skies and 17 lives ended - 13 to age, 4 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:405e400000000000,"to":n:4062c00000000000,"text":[s:"In the year 137, when the guild of Runestead watched gleaming metal run from the glowing ore. Iron smithing entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 139, when the guild of Runestead forged the iron into an edge that never dulled. Metal tools entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 141, three huts grew into more, and Alveheim was founded - a place with a name, which is the beginning of belonging.",s:"In the year 139, Ask II began never fells living trees, and others watched, and followed. So The Ban of the Living Trees took hold.",s:"By the year 137, leaving a round stone at the door of every hut had become simply what one does in Majaheim. It merely became true.",s:"By the year 149, believing the deep iron angers the ancestors had become simply what one does in Runestead. No council voted.",s:"By the year 149, never fells living trees had become simply what one does in Runestead. No one decided this.",s:"And in the year 145, what had been habit became holy: The Way of the Water was born, though none could say when reverence had replaced routine.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 126, Embla — the last soul who understood tin — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 139, Loke II the Voice of Frejaheim — the last soul who understood copper — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 146, Loke II the Voice of Frejaheim — the last soul who understood copper — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 146, Loke II the Voice of Frejaheim — the last soul who understood copper — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 146, Loke II the Voice of Frejaheim — the last soul who understood copper — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Yet in the year 125 it returned - tin, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"In the year 121, Loke II began seeing the world differently - believing unseen wills move all things. Where others saw patterns, they felt a will behind them.",s:"The winter of year 129 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 141 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Vera was known as Vera the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Selma was known as Selma the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Rune II was known as Rune II the Rekindler.",s:"From that day on, Alve II was known as Alve II the Founder.",s:"From that day on, Eira II was known as Eira II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Tuva II was known as Tuva II the Voice of Alveheim.",s:"From that day on, Liv II was known as Liv II the Voice of Alveheim.",s:"From that day on, Loke II was known as Loke II the Voice of Frejaheim.",s:"From that day on, Nanna II was known as Nanna II the Voice of Frejaheim.",s:"From that day on, Ronja II was known as Ronja II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"Otto is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"In Runestead, no one remembers why one goes on whistling to greet the morning. Not even they do. One simply does.",s:"Torv II is gone. But someone still hums at first light. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ylva II is gone. But someone still always the first to fall asleep. No one asks why it began.",s:"Vidar II is gone. But someone still always the first to fall asleep. No one asks why it began.",s:"Tuva II the Voice of Alveheim is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Torv II the Voice of Frejaheim is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Loke II the Voice of Frejaheim is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Signe II is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"Sten II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ylva II is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Signe II reached Alveheim. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"The chronicle notes, without explanation, that Signe II picks a flower every spring and puts it somewhere no one sees. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Vera speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Selma speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Vera's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Selma's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Eira II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Alveheim, the people have begun to listen when Tuva II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Alveheim is without a leader — Tuva II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Alveheim, the people have begun to listen when Liv II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Frejaheim is without a leader — Torv II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Frejaheim, the people have begun to listen when Loke II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Frejaheim is without a leader — Loke II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Frejaheim, the people have begun to listen when Nanna II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Ronja II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Alveheim, the giving has become a way with a name: The Full Bowl Custom — those who keep the same ways do not let each other starve. No price is asked; the gift itself binds.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 64 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 120 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"The year 139 paid an old debt: Vidar II came for Embla II — an old wrong, not forgotten, paid back in goods and bruises. Blood remembers.",s:"Nor were those the only debts: 22 old wrongs were paid in blood that age.",s:"And 4 times, mourners stood over the fallen and marked a name in their hearts. Grief like that waits.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"15 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Through it all 63 children were born under its skies and 16 lives ended - 12 to age, 4 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4062e00000000000,"to":n:4066800000000000,"text":[s:"The chronicle marks the year 173, when Embla II asked not what the world is but why, and wrote it down. Embla II's reasoned thought entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 176, when Nanna II dressed and fitted stone so it stood without mortar. Nanna II's dry-stone entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 153, Ylva II began never digs the ancestors' iron, and others watched, and followed. So The Ban of the Deep Iron took hold.",s:"By the year 163, never digs the ancestors' iron had become simply what one does in Runestead. It merely became true.",s:"By the year 169, that spilling the blood of your own is forbidden had become simply what one does in Runestead. No council voted.",s:"The year 156 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 160 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 166 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 175 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"In the year 159, Maja II began seeing the world differently - that spilling the blood of your own is forbidden. Where others saw patterns, they felt a will behind them.",s:"The winter of year 153 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 165 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 179 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Sten II was known as Sten II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Ylva II was known as Ylva II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Falk II was known as Falk II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Nanna II was known as Nanna II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"From that day on, Embla II was known as Embla II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Halvar II was known as Halvar II the Oathbreaker.",s:"Nanna II is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Sixten II is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ask II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Liv II the Voice of Alveheim is gone. But someone still hums at first light. No one asks why it began.",s:"Orm II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Alve II the Founder is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Idun II reached Majaheim. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"And in those same years, Ask II picks a flower every spring and puts it somewhere no one sees. It began the year Sten II died. It has not stopped since.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Ronja II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Eira II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Falk II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Nanna II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Alveheim is without a leader — Liv II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Falk II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Frejaheim is without a leader — Nanna II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 21 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 60 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"The year 152 paid an old debt: Alve II came for Loke II — an old wrong, not forgotten, paid back in goods and bruises. Blood remembers.",s:"Nor were those the only debts: 17 old wrongs were paid in blood that age.",s:"And 3 times, mourners stood over the fallen and marked a name in their hearts. Grief like that waits.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"9 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Through it all 14 children were born under its skies and 25 lives ended - 24 to age, 1 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4066a00000000000,"to":n:406a400000000000,"text":[s:"The chronicle marks the year 183, when Embla II wrote the customs down so all were judged by one measure. Embla II's the judgment entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 183, when Embla II set the knowing to teach the young in one place. Embla II's the lesson entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 183, when Ask II wrote music down so a song could outlive its singer. Ask II's written music entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 186, when the guild of Runestead found the black stone burns hotter than any wood. Coal entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 191, when the guild of Runestead blew molten sand into clear vessels thin as a bubble. Glassblowing entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood storytelling — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood fire — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood pottery — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood rope — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood sharpened stone — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood spear — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood axe — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood writing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood hut — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood kiln — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood brick — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood weaving — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood farming — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood well — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood granary — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood the wheel — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood bow — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood fishing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood music — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood sailing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood medicine — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood calendar — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood counting — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Selma II — the last soul who understood mill — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood glass — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood philosophy — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood masonry — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood law — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood school — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 207, Ask II — the last soul who understood composition — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"The year 184 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 189 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The winter of year 192 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 208 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Freja II was known as Freja II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Eira II was known as Eira II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Ulv II was known as Ulv II the Oathbreaker.",s:"Vidar II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Torv II is gone. But someone still hums at first light. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ask II is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Loke II is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Rune II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Maja II is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Otto II reached Alveheim. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"The chronicle notes, without explanation, that Loke II walks the last few steps home backward. Always. It began the year Torv II the Voice of Frejaheim died. It has not stopped since.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Nanna II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Eira II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Embla II the Oathbreaker speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Embla II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Eira II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 6 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 6 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"The year 181 paid an old debt: Eira II came for Torv II — an old wrong, not forgotten, paid back in goods and bruises. Blood remembers.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"6 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Through it all 20 children were born under its skies and 26 lives ended - 24 to age, 2 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Reformation","from":n:406a600000000000,"to":n:406e000000000000,"text":[s:"It was in the year 237, when Rune II laid stone in a bed so carts ran true in any weather. Rune II's the highway entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 238, when the guild of Runestead raised the arch, and space opened under stone. Architecture entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"By the year 222, pouring water over the grave had become simply what one does in Runestead. It merely became true.",s:"The year 222 brought upheaval: in Runestead, Pouring water over the grave was set aside, and Laying flowers on the grave took its place. The elders muttered; the young did not listen.",s:"The year 223 brought upheaval: in Runestead, Laying flowers on the grave was set aside, and Pouring water over the grave took its place. The elders muttered; the young did not listen.",s:"The winter of year 220 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 235 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Sixten II was known as Sixten II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"From that day on, Bjorn II was known as Bjorn II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Otto II was known as Otto II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"Sixten II the Voice of Ronjastead is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Orm II is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Otto II reached Alveheim. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"It is also remembered that Sten II walks the last few steps home backward. Always. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Sixten II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Bjorn II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Otto II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Bjorn II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Sixten II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Otto II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"The year 225 knew open greed: Saga II set upon Embla II and seized goods — the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"4 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Meanwhile 32 children were born under its skies and 19 lives ended - 16 to age, 3 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:406e200000000000,"to":n:4070e00000000000,"text":[s:"It was in the year 268, when the guild of Runestead carried water across the valley on arches of stone. Aqueduct entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood storytelling — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood fire — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood pottery — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood rope — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood sharpened stone — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood axe — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood writing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood brick — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood weaving — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood farming — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood well — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood granary — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood the wheel — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood fishing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood music — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood sailing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood medicine — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood calendar — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood counting — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Selma II — the last soul who understood mill — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood glass — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood philosophy — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood law — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood school — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood composition — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 266, Ask II — the last soul who understood road — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 268, Ask II — the last soul who understood storytelling — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 268, Ask II — the last soul who understood fire — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 268, Ask II — the last soul who understood pottery — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 268, Ask II — the last soul who understood rope — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 268, Ask II — the last soul who understood sharpened stone — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 268, Ask II — the last soul who understood spear — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 268, Ask II — the last soul who understood axe — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 268, Ask II — the last soul who understood writing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 268, Ask II — the last soul who understood brick — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 268, Ask II — the last soul who understood weaving — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 268, Ask II — the last soul who understood well — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then ca