rever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - brick, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - weaving, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - well, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - the wheel, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - fishing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - music, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - sailing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - medicine, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - calendar, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - counting, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - glass, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - philosophy, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - law, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - school, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 267 it returned - composition, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - storytelling, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - fire, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - pottery, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - rope, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - sharpened stone, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - spear, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - axe, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - writing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - brick, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - weaving, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - well, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - the wheel, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - fishing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - music, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - sailing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - medicine, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - calendar, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - counting, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - glass, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - philosophy, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - law, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - school, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 269 it returned - composition, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"The winter of year 249 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 269 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Ylva II was known as Ylva II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"From that day on, Sten II was known as Sten II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Bjorn II was known as Bjorn II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Freja II was known as Freja II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Orm II was known as Orm II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Vidar II was known as Vidar II the Voice of Alveheim.",s:"From that day on, Selma II was known as Selma II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"Ask II is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Otto II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Freja II the Voice of Majaheim is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ronja II is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Vidar II the Voice of Alveheim is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Bjorn II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Nanna II reached Runestead. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"It is also remembered that Vidar II has begun collecting round stones. No one knows why. It began the year Otto II died. It has not stopped since.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Ylva II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Sten II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Bjorn II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Sten II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Freja II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Bjorn II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Freja II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Ylva II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Orm II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Alveheim, the people have begun to listen when Vidar II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Alveheim is without a leader — Vidar II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Selma II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 8 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 3 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"The year 265 paid an old debt: Orm II came for Kare II — an old wrong, not forgotten, answered at last. Blood remembers.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"5 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Meanwhile 43 children were born under its skies and 18 lives ended - 12 to age, 6 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4070f00000000000,"to":n:4072c00000000000,"text":[s:"The winter of year 282 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 298 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Falk II was known as Falk II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Freja II was known as Freja II the Voice of Alveheim.",s:"Embla II is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Idun II is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Signe II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Sten II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Eira II is gone. But someone still always the first to fall asleep. No one asks why it began.",s:"Maja II is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Saga II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Rune II reached Majaheim. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"And in those same years, Freja II has begun collecting round stones. No one knows why. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Selma II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Falk II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Falk II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Alveheim, the people have begun to listen when Freja II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 6 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 3 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"2 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"In these years 41 children were born under its skies and 11 lives ended - 10 to age, 1 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4072d00000000000,"to":n:4074a00000000000,"text":[s:"The chronicle marks the year 308, when the guild of Runestead worked iron in a coal-hot fire until it took a keener soul. Steel entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 313, when the guild of Runestead stamped a fixed weight of metal all agreed to trust. Coinage entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"By the year 326, humming together as the sun rises had become simply what one does in Runestead. No one decided this.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood storytelling — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood fire — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood pottery — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood rope — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood sharpened stone — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood spear — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood axe — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood writing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood hut — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood weaving — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood farming — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood well — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood granary — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood the wheel — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood bow — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood fishing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood music — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood sailing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood medicine — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood calendar — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood counting — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood glass — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood philosophy — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood masonry — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood law — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood school — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood composition — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 311, Ask II — the last soul who understood road — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - hut, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - bow, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - masonry, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - farming, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - granary, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - road, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - storytelling, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - fire, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - pottery, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - rope, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - sharpened stone, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - spear, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - axe, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - writing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - weaving, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - well, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - the wheel, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - fishing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - music, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - sailing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - medicine, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - calendar, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - counting, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - glass, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - philosophy, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - law, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - school, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 310 it returned - composition, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - mill, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - brick, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - storytelling, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - fire, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - pottery, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - rope, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - sharpened stone, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - spear, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - writing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - granary, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - bow, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - fishing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - music, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - sailing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - medicine, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - calendar, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - masonry, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - law, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - school, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 326 it returned - road, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 328 it returned - composition, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 329 it returned - kiln, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 329 it returned - axe, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 329 it returned - hut, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 329 it returned - weaving, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 329 it returned - farming, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 329 it returned - well, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 329 it returned - the wheel, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 329 it returned - counting, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 329 it returned - glass, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 329 it returned - philosophy, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"The year 319 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 325 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The winter of year 310 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 322 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Orm II was known as Orm II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Sten II was known as Sten II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Nanna II was known as Nanna II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Freja II was known as Freja II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Kare II was known as Kare II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"From that day on, Saga II was known as Saga II the Voice of Alveheim.",s:"From that day on, Selma II was known as Selma II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"Rune II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Orm II the Voice of Majaheim is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ronja II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Kare II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Freja II the Voice of Alveheim is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Freja II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Bjorn II is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Sixten II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Idun II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Sixten II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Sten II the Voice of Majaheim is gone. But someone still always the first to fall asleep. No one asks why it began.",s:"Maja II is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Orm II the Voice of Runestead is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"Otto II reached Majaheim. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"And in those same years, Eira II carries a stick everywhere. It is never used for anything. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Orm II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Orm II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Alveheim is without a leader — Freja II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Sten II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Kare II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Sten II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Orm II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Alveheim, the people have begun to listen when Saga II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Kare II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Selma II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 10 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 6 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"The year 328 paid an old debt: Falk II came for Kare II the Voice of Ronjastead — an old wrong, not forgotten, paid back in goods and bruises. Blood remembers.",s:"Nor were those the only debts: 3 old wrongs were paid in blood that age.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"12 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Meanwhile 108 children were born under its skies and 31 lives ended - 24 to age, 7 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4074b00000000000,"to":n:4076800000000000,"text":[s:"The chronicle marks the year 344, when the guild of Runestead gathered writings and studied them as a life's work. Scholarship entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 347, when Loke II raised a house for the sacred and gathered the faithful in it. Loke II's sacred house entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"By the year 334, carrying a stick one never uses had become simply what one does in Runestead. It merely became true.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 331, Ask II — the last soul who understood fire — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 331, Ask II — the last soul who understood pottery — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 331, Ask II — the last soul who understood spear — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 331, Ask II — the last soul who understood writing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 331, Ask II — the last soul who understood bow — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 331, Ask II — the last soul who understood fishing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 331, Ask II — the last soul who understood sailing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 331, Ask II — the last soul who understood calendar — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 331, Ask II — the last soul who understood counting — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 331, Ask II — the last soul who understood philosophy — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 331, Ask II — the last soul who understood school — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood storytelling — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood rope — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood sharpened stone — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood axe — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood hut — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood kiln — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood brick — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood weaving — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood farming — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood well — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood granary — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood the wheel — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood music — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood medicine — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Selma II — the last soul who understood mill — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 332, Ask II — the last soul who understood glass — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in