iving Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 343 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 344 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 344 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 346 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 348 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 349 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 351 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 352 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 353 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 355 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 358 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 358 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 359 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 359 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The winter of year 344 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 357 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Signe II was known as Signe II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Sixten II was known as Sixten II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"From that day on, Liv II was known as Liv II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Ask II was known as Ask II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Ronja II was known as Ronja II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Ronja II was known as Ronja II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Signe II was known as Signe II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Bjorn II was known as Bjorn II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Sixten II was known as Sixten II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Tuva II was known as Tuva II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Halvar II was known as Halvar II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Ylva II was known as Ylva II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Sten II was known as Sten II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Disa II was known as Disa II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Idun II was known as Idun II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Vidar II was known as Vidar II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Ulv II was known as Ulv II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Vidar II was known as Vidar II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Idun II was known as Idun II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Signe II was known as Signe II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Tuva II was known as Tuva II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Torv II was known as Torv II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Kare II was known as Kare II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"Sten II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Otto II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Selma II the Voice of Ronjastead is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Vera II is gone. But someone still hums at first light. No one asks why it began.",s:"Liv II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Liv II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Bjorn II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Bjorn II the Voice of Runestead is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Freja II the Oathbreaker is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"Eira II is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"Nanna II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ask II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Halvar II the Voice of Majaheim is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Tuva II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Torv II reached Majaheim. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"It is also remembered that Nanna II whistles every morning, whether the morning deserves it or not. It began the year Vera II died. It has not stopped since.",s:"Alveheim is without a leader — Saga II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Selma II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Sixten II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Bjorn II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Sixten II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Halvar II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Bjorn II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Disa II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Disa II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Vidar II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Kare II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Halvar II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 24 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 8 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"The year 339 paid an old debt: Sixten II the Voice of Ronjastead came for Ronja II — an old wrong, not forgotten, paid back in goods and bruises. Blood remembers.",s:"Nor were those the only debts: 2 old wrongs were paid in blood that age.",s:"Otto II mourns Freja II — and does not forget whose hand it was. Grief like that does not fade; it waits.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"25 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Meanwhile 57 children were born under its skies and 31 lives ended - 28 to age, 3 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4076900000000000,"to":n:4078600000000000,"text":[s:"In the year 361, when the guild of Runestead ground clear glass until it bent light to the eye. Optics entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 363, Ask II — the last soul who understood glassblowing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 385, Ask II — the last soul who understood temple — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Yet in the year 362 it returned - glassblowing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 364 it returned - glassblowing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 388 it returned - temple, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"The year 362 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 363 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 368 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 368 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 371 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 374 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 380 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 382 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 383 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The winter of year 373 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 390 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Kare II was known as Kare II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Nanna II was known as Nanna II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Ask II was known as Ask II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Falk II was known as Falk II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Ronja II was known as Ronja II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Eira II was known as Eira II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Torv II was known as Torv II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Tuva II was known as Tuva II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Kare II was known as Kare II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Selma II was known as Selma II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"Ylva II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Rune II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ask II is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Tuva II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Maja II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Orm II is gone. But someone still hums at first light. No one asks why it began.",s:"Nanna II the Oathbreaker is gone. But someone still hums at first light. No one asks why it began.",s:"Rune II is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ask II the Oathbreaker is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Vera II is gone. But someone still always the first to fall asleep. No one asks why it began.",s:"Nanna II the Oathbreaker is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Selma II is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"Saga II is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Signe II the Oathbreaker is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Signe II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Kare II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Sixten II reached Majaheim. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"The chronicle notes, without explanation, that Nanna II always sits farthest from the fire. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Vidar II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Nanna II the Oathbreaker speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Nanna II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Kare II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Selma II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 24 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 22 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"Eira II mourns Saga II — and does not forget whose hand it was. Grief like that does not fade; it waits.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"13 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"In these years 71 children were born under its skies and 48 lives ended - 43 to age, 5 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4078700000000000,"to":n:407a400000000000,"text":[s:"It was in the year 412, when the guild of Runestead set great sails to catch the wind and turn the stones. Windmill entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 411, Selma II — the last soul who understood mill — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"The year 417 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The year 419 is remembered darkly: The Ban of the Living Trees was broken out of desperation, and the guilt of it did not wash away.",s:"The winter of year 406 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 420 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Loke II was known as Loke II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Ylva II was known as Ylva II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Ulv II was known as Ulv II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Selma II was known as Selma II the Voice of Alveheim.",s:"From that day on, Idun II was known as Idun II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"From that day on, Eira II was known as Eira II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Ulv II was known as Ulv II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Sixten II was known as Sixten II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Bjorn II was known as Bjorn II the Oathbreaker.",s:"From that day on, Nanna II was known as Nanna II the Oathbreaker.",s:"Freja II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ronja II is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ylva II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Alve II is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"Kare II the Oathbreaker is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Rune II is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Embla II is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ylva II is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Sixten II is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Otto II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Vidar II is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"Embla II is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Idun II the Oathbreaker is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Eira II the Voice of Runestead is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Signe II the Oathbreaker is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Sten II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Otto II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Idun II the Voice of Ronjastead is gone. But someone still always the first to fall asleep. No one asks why it began.",s:"Nanna II is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Maja II is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Freja II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Torv II the Oathbreaker is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Signe II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Selma II is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Orm II is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Alve II reached Majaheim. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"And in those same years, Signe II stops at the same strange stone every day, and looks at it. As Otto II did before them. No one decided this.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Loke II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Ylva II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Ylva II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Loke II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Ulv II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Alveheim, the people have begun to listen when Selma II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Selma II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Idun II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Ulv II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Eira II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Eira II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Alveheim is without a leader — Selma II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Idun II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Ulv II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Sixten II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Sixten II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 21 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 9 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"The year 406 paid an old debt: Otto II came for Liv II — an old wrong, not forgotten, paid back in goods and bruises. Blood remembers.",s:"Nor were those the only debts: 2 old wrongs were paid in blood that age.",s:"And 2 times, mourners stood over the fallen and marked a name in their hearts. Grief like that waits.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"10 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Through it all 46 children were born under its skies and 62 lives ended - 54 to age, 8 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:407a500000000000,"to":n:407c200000000000,"text":[s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood storytelling — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood fire — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood pottery — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood rope — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood sharpened stone — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood spear — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood axe — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood writing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood hut — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood kiln — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood brick — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood weaving — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood farming — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood well — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 427, Ask II — the last soul who understood granary — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: