efused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - philosophy, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - law, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - school, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - scholarship, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - rope, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - sharpened stone, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - axe, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - hut, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - brick, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - weaving, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - farming, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - the wheel, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - music, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - masonry, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 497 it returned - temple, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 499 it returned - spear, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 499 it returned - pottery, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 499 it returned - bow, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 499 it returned - fishing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 499 it returned - sailing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 499 it returned - medicine, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 499 it returned - counting, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 499 it returned - law, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 499 it returned - school, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 499 it returned - scholarship, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - well, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - composition, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - glassblowing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - writing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - fire, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - philosophy, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - brick, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - the wheel, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - music, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - storytelling, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - pottery, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - rope, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - sharpened stone, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - weaving, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - farming, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - granary, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - bow, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - fishing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - sailing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - medicine, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - counting, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - law, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 506 it returned - scholarship, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"The winter of year 485 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 497 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 509 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Alve II was known as Alve II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"From that day on, Sten II was known as Sten II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Idun II was known as Idun II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Kare II was known as Kare II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"From that day on, Eira II was known as Eira II the Voice of Alveheim.",s:"Nanna II is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Selma II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Saga II is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ylva II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Halvar II is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ask II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Sten II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ronja II is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Tuva II is gone. But someone still always the first to fall asleep. No one asks why it began.",s:"Selma II is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Kare II the Voice of Ronjastead is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Freja II is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Selma II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Sten II reached Alveheim. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"It is also remembered that Selma II always takes the long way home, even in rain. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Alve II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Sten II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Idun II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Alve II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Kare II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Idun II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Alveheim, the people have begun to listen when Eira II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Alveheim is without a leader — Eira II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Kare II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Sten II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 10 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 2 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"Ronja II mourns Selma II — and does not forget whose hand it was. Grief like that does not fade; it waits.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"10 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Meanwhile 80 children were born under its skies and 34 lives ended - 29 to age, 5 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:407ff00000000000,"to":n:4080e00000000000,"text":[s:"It was in the year 514, when the guild of Runestead joined scholars and students into a lasting house of learning. University entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 531, when Alve II tested the guess against the world and kept only what held. Alve II's experiment entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - kiln, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - road, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - optics, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - calendar, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - glass, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - hut, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - masonry, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - spear, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - axe, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - school, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - storytelling, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - fire, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - pottery, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - rope, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - sharpened stone, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - writing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - weaving, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - farming, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - well, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - granary, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - the wheel, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - bow, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - fishing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - music, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - sailing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - medicine, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - counting, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - philosophy, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - law, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - composition, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - glassblowing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 516 it returned - scholarship, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 517 it returned - temple, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 517 it returned - brick, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 518 it returned - mill, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"The winter of year 521 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 536 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Sixten II was known as Sixten II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Idun II was known as Idun II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Sten II was known as Sten II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Otto II was known as Otto II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"From that day on, Ulv II was known as Ulv II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"Signe II is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Rune II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ylva II is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Tuva II is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Kare II is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Saga II is gone. But someone still always the first to fall asleep. No one asks why it began.",s:"Liv II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Torv II is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Otto II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Otto II the Voice of Ronjastead is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Alve II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Halvar II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ulv II the Voice of Majaheim is gone. But someone still hums at first light. No one asks why it began.",s:"Signe II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Maja II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Torv II reached Majaheim. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"And in those same years, Liv II has started humming at first light. It began the year Saga II died. It has not stopped since.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Sixten II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Idun II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Sixten II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Sten II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Otto II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Sten II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Idun II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Ulv II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Otto II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Ulv II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 16 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 2 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"5 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"In these years 52 children were born under its skies and 30 lives ended - 27 to age, 3 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4080e80000000000,"to":n:4081d00000000000,"text":[s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 562, Ask II — the last soul who understood writing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 562, Selma II — the last soul who understood mill — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 562, Ask II — the last soul who understood glassblowing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 562, Ask II — the last soul who understood optics — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 566, Ask II — the last soul who understood glassblowing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Yet in the year 565 it returned - writing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 565 it returned - glassblowing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"The winter of year 549 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 561 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Ronja II was known as Ronja II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Bjorn II was known as Bjorn II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Falk II was known as Falk II the Voice of Alveheim.",s:"From that day on, Sixten II was known as Sixten II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"From that day on, Maja II was known as Maja II the Voice of Alveheim.",s:"Bjorn II is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Nanna II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Selma II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Liv II is gone. But someone still hums at first light. No one asks why it began.",s:"Embla II is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Rune II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ronja II the Voice of Majaheim is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Idun II is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ask II is gone. But someone still hums at first light. No one asks why it began.",s:"Bjorn II the Voice of Runestead is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Bjorn II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"In Majaheim, no one remembers why one goes on leaving a round stone at the door of every hut. Not even they do. One simply does.",s:"Rune II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Maja II the Voice of Alveheim is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Kare II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Kare II came home from Alveheim carrying more than they left with. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"And in those same years, Bjorn II counts the others every evening before sleep. It began the year Nanna II died. It has not stopped since.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Ronja II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Bjorn II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Ronja II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Alveheim, the people have begun to listen when Falk II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Bjorn II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Sixten II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Alveheim is without a leader — Falk II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Alveheim, the people have begun to listen when Maja II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Alveheim is without a leader — Maja II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 7 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 4 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"5 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Meanwhile 75 children were born under its skies and 53 lives ended - 43 to age, 10 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4081d80000000000,"to":n:4082c00000000000,"text":[s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 575, Ask II — the last soul who understood glassblowing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 575, Ask II — the last soul who understood optics — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood spear — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood kiln — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood brick — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood weaving — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood farming — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood well — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood granary — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood the wheel — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood fishing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood sailing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood medicine — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood counting — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood glass — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood law — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood composition — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood road — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood glassblowing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood science — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 586, Ask II — the last soul who understood university — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 591, Ask II — the last soul who understood writing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Yet in the year 574 it returned - optics, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 574 it returned - glassblowing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 576 it returned - glassblowing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 587 it returned - kiln, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 587 it returned - weaving, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 588 it returned - glass, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 588 it returned - law, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 589 it returned - brick, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 589 it returned - well, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 589 it returned - counting, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 589 it returned - composition, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 592 it returned - university, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 594 it returned - medicine, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 597 it returned - writing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"The winter of year 574 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 595 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Otto II was known as Otto II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"From that day on, Idun II was known as Idun II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"Disa II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"Liv II is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Alve II is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Vidar II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Orm II reached Majaheim. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"The chronicle notes, without explanation, that Vidar II picks a flower every spring and puts it somewhere no one sees. It began the year Ylva II died. It has not stopped since.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Sixten II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Otto II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Otto II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Idun II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Hunger turned to theft 14 times in this age — desperate hands in lean seasons, and every one remembered.",s:"Greed walked openly 6 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"3 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Through it all 21 children were born under its skies and 17 lives ended - 16 to age, 1 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4082c80000000000,"to":n:4083b00000000000,"text":[s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 621, Selma II — the last soul who understood mill — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Yet in the year 606 it returned - spear, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 608 it returned - fishing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 609 it returned - sailing, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 615 it returned - road, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"The winter of year 609 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 621 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Vidar II was known as Vidar II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Sten II was known as Sten II the Voice of Ronjastead.",s:"From that day on, Otto II was known as Otto II the Voice of Runestead.",s:"From that day on, Vidar II was known as Vidar II the Voice of Majaheim.",s:"Nanna II is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Nanna II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Halvar II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Vidar II the Voice of Runestead is gone. But someone still always sits farthest from the fire. No one asks why it began.",s:"Falk II is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ulv II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Signe II is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"Maja II is gone. But someone still hums at first light. No one asks why it began.",s:"Sixten II is gone. But someone still collects round stones. For nothing. No one asks why it began.",s:"Vera II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Maja II reached Ronjastead. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"The chronicle notes, without explanation, that Rune II walks the last few steps home backward. Always. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Vidar II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Vidar II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Majaheim is without a leader — Idun II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Ronjastead, the people have begun to listen when Sten II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Runestead, the people have begun to listen when Otto II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Ronjastead is without a leader — Sten II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Majaheim, the people have begun to listen when Vidar II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Runestead is without a leader — Otto II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"Greed walked openly 4 times — the strong taking because the gap was cheaper to close by force.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"One soul, that age, quietly left an old way for a new one.",s:"In these years no children were born and 29 lives ended - 29 to age.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4083b80000000000,"to":n:4084a00000000000,"text":[s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 636, Selma II — the last soul who understood mill — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 636, Ask II the Oathbreaker — the last soul who understood architecture — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 639, Selma II — the last soul who understood mill — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood fire — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood storytelling — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood pottery — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood writing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood sharpened stone — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood rope — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood spear — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood axe — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood hut — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood bow — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood kiln — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood farming — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood granary — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood brick — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood well — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood weaving — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood the wheel — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood sailing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood fishing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood music — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood counting — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood calendar — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood medicine — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood glass — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood philosophy — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood masonry — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood law — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood school — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 640, Ask II — the last soul who understood composition — died, and the knowledge 